# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* into the bundle at build time.
#
# ⚠ This file is what the LOCALLY-SERVED bundle uses. `eas.json` env only applies
# to bundles EAS itself builds — so without this, an app running against local
# Metro falls back to `sandbox` and registers the wrong environment (ADR 0026).
#
# `production` is right for every profile that can obtain a token: EAS internal
# distribution is ad-hoc, and ad-hoc, TestFlight and App Store all carry
# `aps-environment: production`.
#
# ⚠ Override to `sandbox` ONLY for a build made with a genuine *Development*
# provisioning profile (e.g. `npx expo run:ios` signed in Xcode with a dev profile).
EXPO_PUBLIC_APNS_ENV=production
